# DJ Website — Project Context for Cursor

## Stack
- Next.js 14+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Content: Sanity (or Contentful) for presskit bio/photos/tech rider
- Payments: Stripe Checkout for merch (no custom cart state — use Stripe-hosted checkout)
- Booking: form → Resend (email) OR Calendly embed — no custom calendar/scheduling logic
- Radio: embedded player only (Mixcloud / SoundCloud / Azuracast) — never build custom streaming infra

## Site map (do not add pages outside this list without asking)
- `/`            — hero, latest mix embed, upcoming shows list
- `/presskit`    — bio, photo gallery, tech rider, downloadable press kit (PDF/ZIP)
- `/book`        — booking form or embedded scheduler
- `/merch`       — Stripe-powered product grid + checkout
- `/radio`       — embedded live/past sets player

## Conventions
- Server Components by default; only use `"use client"` when the component needs interactivity (forms, players, cart buttons)
- Keep each route's logic self-contained in its `app/<route>/` folder — don't cross-import merch logic into presskit, etc.
- Styling: Tailwind utility classes only, no separate CSS files unless truly global
- Env vars go in `.env.local`, never hardcode API keys (Stripe, Sanity, Resend)
- Forms: validate with `zod`, submit via server actions where possible instead of client-side fetch to custom API routes

## Build order (follow this sequence)
1. Layout + nav/footer, deploy skeleton to Vercel
2. `/presskit` (static content, quick win)
3. `/radio` (embed only)
4. `/book` (form + email or Calendly embed)
5. `/merch` (Stripe products + checkout + webhook) — build last, most complex

## Out of scope for v1
- Custom cart/checkout UI (use Stripe Checkout redirect)
- Custom calendar/availability system (use Calendly/Cal.com embed)
- Self-hosted audio streaming server
